      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Because Git keeps a history of commits. Even if you delete the file in a new commit, the API key may still exist in earlier commits.\nSomeone might access that old commit, a fork, a clone, or a cached copy and recover the key.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Because Git keeps a history of commits. Even if you delete the file in a new commit, the API key may still exist in earlier commits.\nSomeone might access that old commit, a fork, a clone, or a cached copy and recover the key.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FyxCb1TOkkIxrdwrrZRjn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -204.4339478978738,
      "y": 6753.444717680277,
      "width": 1364,
      "height": 75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
      "backgroundColor": "#000000",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Xl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1134406597,
      "version": 482,
      "versionNonce": 260072389,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791633308192,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Revoke or rotate it. This is the most important step.\nRemoving the key from GitHub does not make the old key safe again. Generate a new key and update your application to use it.\n If the key belongs to a third-party service, use that service's dashboard to revoke or regenerate it.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Revoke or rotate it. This is the most important step.\nRemoving the key from GitHub does not make the old key safe again. Generate a new key and update your application to use it.\n If the key belongs to a third-party service, use that service's dashboard to revoke or regenerate it.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1ktY43s7WYhLBln8uKwi_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -183.77702078180556,
      "y": 7087.024753642515,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
      "backgroundColor": "#000000",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Xt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1536249259,
      "version": 602,
      "versionNonce": 643863531,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791633352811,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Store secrets in a .env file instead of directly in your code.\n- Add .env to .gitignore.\n- Commit an .env.example file with placeholder values, not real secrets.\n- Use secret-scanning tools, such as GitHub secret scanning or a pre-commit tool like Gitleaks.\n- Keep API keys in your deployment platform's environment variables or secret manager.\n\nFor example, instead of this:\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Store secrets in a .env file instead of directly in your code.\n- Add .env to .gitignore.\n- Commit an .env.example file with placeholder values, not real secrets.\n- Use secret-scanning tools, such as GitHub secret scanning or a pre-commit tool like Gitleaks.\n- Keep API keys in your deployment platform's environment variables or secret manager.\n\nFor example, instead of this:\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
